{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q002_mazg_hise_remote_homology","answer":"SCOPe 2.08 supports remote homology: d1vmga_ and d1y6xa1 belong to different families within the same superfamily, indicating probable common ancestry rather than merely a similar fold.

Specifically, d1vmga_ (sunid 113676; PDB 1vmg, chain A) belongs to the MazG-like family a.204.1.2 (sunid 116993). d1y6xa1 (sunid 122676; PDB 1y6x, chain A, residues 7–93) belongs to the HisE-like (PRA-PH) family a.204.1.4 (sunid 140797). Both fall in the all-alpha NTP pyrophosphatases superfamily a.204.1 (sunid 101386), the identically named fold a.204 (sunid 101385), and the All alpha proteins class a (sunid 46456). The superfamily assignment supplies the evolutionary inference; fold or class membership alone would not establish homology. Their distinct families reflect a more remote relationship than shared family membership.

This classification does not establish identical substrates, catalytic specificity, kinetics, physiological roles, or orthology. In particular, the HisE protein annotation—phosphoribosyl-ATP pyrophosphatase—cannot be transferred to d1vmga_, whose SCOPe protein entry is labeled hypothetical protein SSo12199 (SSo3215). Conversely, MazG-associated broad nucleotide hydrolysis or nucleotide-pool maintenance roles cannot be assigned to d1y6xa1 solely from shared superfamily membership. The superfamily name suggests a broad biochemical relationship, not experimentally demonstrated activity for every member. Specific functional transfer requires independent biochemical evidence, supported by active-site conservation, substrate/ligand recognition, and biological context. Either domain may inform comparison of the conserved structural core, but using it as a template for the other's substrate specificity or detailed active-site geometry requires additional validation.","evidence_used":["/api/v1/","/api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/d1vmga_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/d1y6xa1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/113676","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/122676","/api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/a.204.1.2","/api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/a.204.1.4","/api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/a.204.1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/a.204","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/116994","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/140801","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/46456","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/116993","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/140798","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/140797"]}]}
